Noting that his progress was affected by the collarbone injury he suffered after an ATV accident late last year &#8212; which left him temporarily unable to exercise &#8212; the Grammy winner weighed himself on camera, revealing he&#8217;d gained about 12 pounds over the past few months. But that&#8217;s not stopping him from getting back on track. Also in the vlog, he shows off how he&#8217;s been running frequent 5Ks lately to train for his ultimate goal of running his first marathon in New York City this November.

Jelly has been in the process of slimming down for a few years now, and in January, he celebrated losing nearly 300 pounds by posing on the cover of Men&#8217;s Health . &#8220;I started treating my food addiction like what it was: an addiction,&#8221; he told the publication at the time. &#8220;It started changing everything for me &#8230; really looking at the source of why I was eating. What was I eating for?”

